# PART 3: YOUR VALUE PROPOSITION

## Your Core Value (What You Deliver)

```
Understand requirements
  ↓
Communicate clearly
  ↓
Build reliable solutions
  ↓
Document everything
  ↓
Deliver professionally
```

Wave doesn't need another developer. They need reliability.

## What Wave Gets From You

1. **You understand logistics** — Transportation, dispatch, real-time systems are familiar
2. **You communicate** — You ask questions, define success, flag blockers early
3. **You build maintainably** — Code is readable, documented, handoff-ready
4. **You reduce risk** — You clarify before committing, test thoroughly, don't over-promise
5. **You're professional** — Responsive, work within their process, make their team better

## Your Three Key Messages (Memorize These)

### Opening
"I focus on understanding what you're trying to solve, building reliable solutions, and making sure your team can maintain and extend the work. I communicate clearly, document decisions, and respect your constraints."

### Core Positioning
"I take unclear business requirements, organize them into a clear plan, communicate expectations upfront, build the solution reliably, document everything, and deliver something your team can maintain and scale."

### Closing
"I'm excited about Wave's mission. Looking forward to learning more about what success looks like in 30, 60, and 90 days if we work together."

## What NOT to Say Tomorrow

❌ "I'm an AI expert" (Wave doesn't care about your tools)
❌ "I can build anything" (sounds unreliable)
❌ "This will take 3 weeks" (before understanding requirements)
❌ "I'll need lots of access" (security concern)
❌ Talk too much (listen more)

## What TO Say Tomorrow

✅ "I understand transportation logistics and dispatch challenges"
✅ "I'll start by understanding your current system and pain points"
✅ "I focus on reliable, documented, maintainable solutions"
✅ "I work well with clear success criteria and regular communication"
✅ "I'm comfortable with real-time systems, payments, and compliance"

