# PART 7: YOUR EXECUTION FRAMEWORK (How You'll Work)

## Your Contractor Approach

### Phase 1: Understand (Week 1)
```
- Audit current system (architecture, code, team)
- Document workflows and pain points
- Interview key stakeholders
- Identify quick wins vs. major refactors
- Present findings + recommendation
```

### Phase 2: Plan (Week 1-2)
```
- Design solution with stakeholder input
- Define success criteria
- Estimate effort and timeline
- Get written approval
- Create detailed implementation plan
```

### Phase 3: Build (Weeks 2+)
```
- Implement in small, reviewable chunks
- Daily progress communication
- Weekly demos of working software
- Incorporate feedback immediately
- Maintain test coverage (80%+)
```

### Phase 4: Deliver (Final weeks)
```
- Complete documentation
- Train team on new system
- Set up monitoring and alerting
- Handle day-1 issues
- Create runbook for operations
```

### Phase 5: Handoff
```
- Knowledge transfer session
- Team confirms they can operate system
- Documentation is current
- You're available for questions first week
```

## Your Communication Protocol

**Daily**: Slack message (5 min) - what done, what's next, blockers
**Weekly**: 30-min standup - demo working feature, get feedback
**Blockers**: Flag immediately, don't wait for standup
**Decisions**: Written, with reasoning, so team can make same call later
**Code**: Reviewed with team, merged to main daily

## What You'll Track

- Lines of code written (velocity)
- Tests written (coverage target: 80%+)
- Bugs fixed (quality metric)
- Time spent (est. vs. actual)
- Blockers (risks)
- Team feedback (satisfaction)

